    "modelText": "{\n  \"schemaVersion\": \"week07.student-model/v1\",\n  \"id\": \"week07-student-model\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n  \"slots\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"controls.demand\",\n      \"expressions\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"requiredMoment\",\n          \"expression\": \"\",\n          \"unit\": \"N*m\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"controls.effectiveness\",\n      \"expressions\": [\n        {\n          \"name\": \"dynamicPressure\",\n          \"expression\": \"\",\n          \"unit\": \"Pa\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"deltaCm\",\n          \"expression\": \"\",\n          \"unit\": \"1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"name\": \"deltaMoment\",\n          \"expression\": \"\",\n          \"unit\": \"N*m\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}",
    "modelHash": "fnv1a-adee3cf8",
    "fields": {
      "question": {
        "suppliedBy": "instructor",
        "locked": true,
        "text": "Calculate required control moment, elevator moment, and the change with airspeed. Explain whether the nominal response meets +0.12 rad/s²."
      },
      "system": {
        "suppliedBy": "instructor",
        "locked": true,
        "text": "Illustrative planar pitch model. Aircraft geometry, integration, force conversion and constraints are supplied."
      },
      "representation": {
        "suppliedBy": "instructor",
        "locked": true,
        "text": "Body axes forward/right/down. Positive pitch moment nose-up. Positive Fz downward. Positive elevator trailing edge down. Reference/CG X=0 m; tail X=-3 m."
      },
      "physics": {
        "suppliedBy": "student",
        "locked": false,
        "text": "Let Cg be the pivot point.\nthe downward force (-) aft of Cg is equal to upward force(+) front of Cg because both provide torque in the same direction (+) in respect to y axis.\n\ncan also use another approach,\ndeltaCm=Cm_alpha*alpha/delta_alpha . Since Cm_alpha/delta_alpha is negative and alpha is negative (-)*(-) =(+) = nose up"
      },
      "assumptions": {
        "suppliedBy": "student",
        "locked": false,
        "text": "Cmδ is linear in our range of calculation compare to alpha"
      },
      "inputs": {
        "suppliedBy": "instructor",
        "locked": true,
        "text": "Iy=5000 kg·m²; target=+0.12 rad/s²; competing=-750 N-m; density=1.225 kg/m³; V=40 m/s; S=16 m²; chord=1.5 m; Cmδ=-0.8/rad; elevator=-5°. Inputs are illustrative, not calibrated."
      },
      "model": {
        "suppliedBy": "student",
        "locked": false,
        "text": "Demand = Iy*target - competing\nq∞ = 0.5*density*V^2\nMoment = Cmδ * q∞ * S * chord\n\n\nDemand will be calculated\nall known"
      },
      "prediction": {
        "suppliedBy": "student",
        "locked": false,
        "text": "deltaCm=Cm_alpha*alpha/delta_alpha . Since Cm_alpha/delta_alpha is negative and alpha is negative (-)*(-) =(+) = nose up"
      },
